# Copy to .gitignore in a BREAD board repo.

# ── KiCad 10 local history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KiCad 10 added a Local History feature (common/local_history.cpp). On first
# save it creates <project>/.history/ and runs git_repository_init() on it — so
# it is a NESTED GIT REPOSITORY holding KiCad's own undo history.
#
# KiCad writes a .gitignore *inside* .history/, but that governs what KiCad's
# history repo snapshots. It does nothing for the board repo, which sees
# .history/ as an embedded repository and reports it untracked. Committing it
# would put a broken gitlink in the repo.
#
# It is machine-local scratch state. Never commit it.
.history/

# ── KiCad backup and swap files ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bck
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.sch-bak
*~
*-backups/

# ── KiCad autosave ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.sav

# ── Machine-local KiCad configuration ────────────────────────────────────────
# Library tables hold absolute paths, so they differ per machine and must not be
# committed. CI generates them from KiCad-Master-Lib's committed tables via
# scripts/write_project_lib_tables.py; do the same locally.
fp-info-cache
sym-lib-table
fp-lib-table
design-block-lib-table

# Project-LOCAL settings: KiCad rewrites this on every open (open sheet, zoom,
# selection filter, ...). It is per-developer scratch, not design intent, and
# tracking it means the working tree goes dirty every time anyone opens the
# board. If it is already tracked: git rm --cached hardware/*.kicad_prl
*.kicad_prl

# ── KiBot output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Generated/

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.swp
working/
